A leaderboard.

A player has a name (text) and a score (a whole number).

The ranking of some players (a list of players) is a list of texts:
its name for each player in the players sorted by its score, largest first.

The best of some players (a list of players) is a whole number:
the largest of its score for each player in the players.

Suppose ana is a player with name "Ana" and score 30.
Suppose bo is a player with name "Bo" and score 50.
Suppose cy is a player with name "Cy" and score 10.
For example, the ranking of a list of ana, bo and cy joined with "," is "Bo,Ana,Cy".
For example, the best of a list of ana, bo and cy is 50.
